WEBVTT

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.950
Ensign Kou Uraki has experienced
the ordeal of real combat.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.820
He has faced the man
who stole Gundam Unit 2.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.420
Anavel Gato.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.790
The Zeon ace pilot who struck fear
in the hearts of Federation soldiers.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.390
A shudder that chills the
fingers and dries the throat.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.130
And the departing souls of friends.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:33.800
With Uraki looking on, Unit 2
vanished into the morning mist.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.810
Uraki's first battle
is stained with disgrace.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:01:02.540
Mobile Suit Gundam 0083

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:08.490
shourisha nado inai tatakai ni tsukare hate
There's no winner of this fight as I collapse, now exhausted.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.460
hoshizora o miageru
I look up to the stars above...

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.130
naku koto mo kanawanai
...and don't even have the strength to cry.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:19.500
I don't need kinou nado iranai
I don't need, don't need yesterday anymore.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:25.780
I don't need kuchi hateta yume mo
I don't need dreams that have crumbled away.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.010
I got a burning heart!

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.010
mune o tsuranuku suriru wo
I just wanna keep on running!

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:37.850
tada oi kakete hashiri tsuzuketai
Just chasing the thrill that's shooting through my heart!

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:42.520
kotoba ni dekinai omoi ga
Feelings that you just can't describe with words...

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:50.410
kogoeta kokoro sae atsuku saseru
...are enough to ignite even a frozen heart!

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.070
I got a burning love!

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.140
aoku kagayaku honoo de
Burning with shining blue fire.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:01.860
kono hoshizora o ooi tsukusu toki made
Fire that'll spread until it covers all the stars in the sky.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.220
I got a burning heart!

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.350
ai wa kodoku na tatakai
Love is such a lonely battle.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:15.160
kono sekai made moyashi tsukusu no ka
But is it one that will consume the world in flames?

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:40.280
INTO BATTLE, ALBION!

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.620
<i>This is Captain Synapse</i>
<i>of the</i> Albion.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.960
Ensign Kou Uraki, sir!

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:21.560
I had no excuse to take
Unit 1 without permission...

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:22.860
<i>What's your impression</i>
<i>of the prototype?</i>

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.900
Huh? Uh...

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.170
The power and maneuverability make
it an excellent mobile suit, sir.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.670
<i>I see. Good work.</i>
<i>Get some rest.</i>

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.300
Aye, sir!

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.010
Captain, we have a message
coming in from Jaburo.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.110
Route it to the main monitor.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.390
<i>...and give #13 priority!</i>
<i>Tell them I said so!</i>

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.130
<i>Forgive the wait, Captain.</i>
<i>How go the repairs to the Albion?</i>

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:55.930
Ah, Admiral Kowen. It'll take
another 7 or 8 hours, sir.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.700
<i>I see.</i>

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.000
Anything on the spy sats?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.410
<i>No, there's no new intelligence.</i>

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.400
<i>The real question is</i>
<i>whether we made things worse...</i>

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.880
<i>...by preventing</i>
<i>their escape into space.</i>

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.010
You mean... You think they
may use the nuke on Jaburo?

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:18.990
<i>Commanders have to assume the</i>
<i>worst possible scenario.</i>

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:22.430
<i>We can't pretend the Antarctic Treaty</i>
<i>will save us from our own warhead.</i>

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:26.330
<i>In any case, I want you to</i>
<i>take charge of the recovery...</i>

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.340
<i>...of the nuke and</i>
<i>the stolen prototype.</i>

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.340
<i>Get the</i> Albion <i>repaired ASAP!</i>

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.870
We'll do our best, sir.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.370
<i>Captain Synapse...</i>

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:41.970
<i>The war is over. But that one</i>
<i>bomb can kill millions more people.</i>

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.110
<i>That weapon must not be used.</i>

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.760
We'll have to reset the regulator
in the secondary jumper, or else...

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.290
Nina!

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.630
Good job, Ensign.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:06.130
I'm sorry, Nina. I didn't keep
my promise to get Unit 2 back.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.010
I've brought Unit 1 back.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.270
Thank you for everything!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.820
He's pretty forthright
for a soldier.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.550
You're right.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:22.210
<i>To all</i> Albion <i>crew members.</i>

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.880
<i>As of today, this ship is</i>
<i>charged with the recovery...</i>

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.520
<i>...of prototype unit 2 and</i>
<i>the stolen nuclear warhead.</i>

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.860
<i>As soon as we have a lead on</i>
<i>where the enemy escaped to...</i>

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.830
<i>...we'll go onto</i>
<i>active operational status.</i>

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.200
<i>All personnel,</i>
<i>prepare to move out.</i>

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.600
Nina, you're a civilian.
You'd better leave the ship.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.610
I can ask the company
about that later.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.940
Right now, checking
out Unit 1 comes first.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.190
Hi! Hey, why so glum?

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.740
It's nothing.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.600
Hold on, Kou.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.570
Cheer up!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.580
I hear they sent us some more
suits and veteran pilots to help.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.080
You fought really well!

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.710
The guy you fought
yesterday was Gato!

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.380
The Nightmare of Solomon
from the One Year War!

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:34.250
Just fighting him and coming back
alive is a real accomplishment!

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.190
Only because the
lieutenant saved me.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.590
You were on your way
to visit him, right?

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.750
Christ, it's hot out! It's the
middle of winter, for God's sake!

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.190
This is the southern
hemisphere, Lieutenant.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.880
Orders are orders,
Monsha, ol' buddy.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:08.450
Hell, I finally get some leave
and they pull me off it for this!

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.930
I was right in
the middle of a date!

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.450
So you keep telling us.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:16.560
Marie isn't gonna wait
for me, God dammit!

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.950
'Scuse me, ladies!

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.580
Any of you free tonight?!

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.780
The guy's hopeless.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:37.020
- Isn't he ever gonna learn?
- Hey! What's the big idea?!

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.930
Is this right?

00:07:57.140 --> 00:08:00.080
Check it out! There it is!

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:03.050
That's the one I'm getting!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.450
They still haven't
chosen you, have they?

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.680
You, down there!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.120
The Gundam is being
serviced right now!

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.560
Keep away from it, please!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.110
Like a rose in fullest bloom...

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.450
C- Can I help you...

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.720
Lieutenant j.g.
Bernard Monsha, my dear!

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.730
I was just stationed here today.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.660
And what might your name be?

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:51.390
Nina Purpleton.
You're pilots, aren't you?

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.590
I suppose you came to see Unit 1.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.470
Ah, but I have eyes
for none but you!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.970
Lieutenant Monsha, if you have no
business here, then please get down.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.410
You're interfering with my work.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.710
I like your personality!
You're my ideal woman!

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.080
Nina!

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.710
Be careful! That guy just
felt up all of my girls!

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.120
He's a total pervert!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:18.650
Wh- Why, you Amazon! You get
in my way and you'll be sorry!

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.120
No, YOU will!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.690
Hold on. We're gonna be
working together from now on.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.100
Let's skip the fights.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:28.430
By the way, is there a Lieutenant
j.g. Burning on this base?

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:32.890
Junior grade? We've got a full
Lieutenant Burning in the med tent.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.570
Something happened to him?!

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:38.240
He was hospitalized after
being injured this morning.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.810
Okay, next!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:54.050
Lieutenant, are you
sure you're not hurt bad?

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.720
Oh, forget it. Those stupid
doctors are just overreacting.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.060
This is...

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.690
...hardly what I'd
call a real injury.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.700
Lieutenant, since the <i>Albion</i> got
those new suits and pilots...

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:09.640
...does that mean they won't
be needing us anymore?

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:13.080
Hm... I'd guess it does.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.780
Then we won't
have to fight anymore.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.080
Lieutenant Burning!

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.950
- Lieutenant!
- Lieutenant!

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.420
You guys!

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:26.050
We heard someone got you, so we
checked the morgue in the basement.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.960
You jerks! I can't believe
you're all still alive!

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:33.430
We're the immortal
04th team, right?

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:35.700
We won't get killed that easy.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:37.100
A get-well gift.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:42.400
Oh, of course! Those reserves
they called in are you guys!

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.410
They transferred us
in for this mission.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.410
Thanks to that, I lost my leave!

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.010
Still, I can't believe that new
suit was stolen so easily.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.650
And I hear someone took
Unit 1 to go after it...

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:57.590
...and they still couldn't
stop it from getting away!

00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:01.690
Well, guess the pilot
was a real screw up.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:04.420
Guess so.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:09.030
It was my team who went after Unit 2.
As leader, it's my responsibility.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.400
Insert foot in mouth...

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.640
These are Ensigns Keith
and Uraki from my team.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.670
You two go collect
Allen's personal effects.

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.110
- Aye, aye!
- Excuse us!

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.680
Those two are still green,
aren't they?

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:31.020
A couple of ensigns
fresh out of the Academy, huh?

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:34.390
Nah, those two may have
a lot of potential.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:37.020
Especially considering the
guy they fought yesterday...

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:38.620
...was the Nightmare of Solomon.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.660
The Nightmare of Solomon?

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.430
He's still alive?

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.370
I don't believe it, Lieutenant.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:48.530
Those two kids went up against
that Zeek bastard, Gato?

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:10.090
Well, I'll do this part, okay?

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:15.430
He always needs time
to get over things...

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.190
Ensign Uraki, entering, sir!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.430
If I... If I had just!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:27.470
If I'd just been
a little better!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:32.440
Damn it all! Damn it all!
Damn it all...

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.490
Good job, Commander!

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:01.060
It looks like everyone at Kimbareid
is looking forward to your arrival!

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:04.440
How long till we reach Africa?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.480
About a week, sir.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:08.450
I see...

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:11.510
I never expected we'd
need to use that thing.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.820
Kou! Are you serious?!

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:23.490
C'mon, Kou, why are you volunteering
for the recovery mission?!

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:29.130
Because I can't just sit
here with my thumb up my ass!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:32.830
So you're going to
purposely risk your life again?!

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.170
Well, if it isn't the ensign.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:50.320
Hold it. I heard you tangled
with the Nightmare of Solomon.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.720
I'm in a hurry, sir.
Excuse me.

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:57.320
Got no time for me, huh?

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:02.300
I get it. Must be busy since
you fought with Gato.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:07.860
Or maybe you didn't, and just
hid till he got away. Huh, kid?

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:11.970
I was saved because of
Lieutenant Burning and Nina!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.310
If I was on my own,
I'd probably be dead now.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.040
That's not true!

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.280
It was your own skill,
Ensign Uraki.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.980
N- Nina...

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.990
This is the data from when
you were piloting Unit 1.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.990
You tapped its
potential far beyond...

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:30.000
...what would be expected from
your first time operating it.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.290
Have faith in yourself,
Ensign Uraki.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.860
You came to just?

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:38.300
Yes.
I brought this to show you.

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:44.300
So, you're an amateur pilot but a
professional with the ladies, huh?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.710
Lieutenant!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.670
Nina, showing us that stuff
doesn't prove a thing.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:53.310
Unit 1 's pilot is
gonna be one of us.

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:58.310
There's no way they're gonna
give it to this rookie pilot!

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:03.350
After all, he let Unit 2
get away, didn't he?

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:06.330
Hey, lay off him.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.160
He's one of Lieutenant
Burning's men, remember?

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.400
Yeah, but he's
still a crappy pilot.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:16.640
But don't worry, I'll take good
care of Unit 1 and Nina.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.640
The kid here can run home...

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:21.910
...and have his mama diaper
him to go beddy-bye!

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:24.410
Lieutenant Monsha!

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:28.050
A pilot with an
ounce of real skill...

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:31.420
...wouldn't guess at someone
else's before seeing it!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:35.830
Ensign Uraki may even be
a better pilot than you are.

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:40.660
Interesting joke...
Well, wanna find out for sure?

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.060
Huh?

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:46.430
If Ensign Uraki manages
to beat me in a fight...

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:50.030
...I'll recommend him
to be the Gundam's pilot.

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:53.270
However! If I win the fight...

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:56.370
...then he never shows his
face in front of us again!

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.470
What do you say?!

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:03.390
I accept! Let me try!

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.750
All right, it's settled, then.

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:10.760
Kou, it's impossible!
He's a veteran pilot!

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:14.360
Keith...
This is my only chance!

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.460
I want to get Unit 2 back,
no matter what!

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.360
Kou...

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:25.840
I'll crush you with no
effort in front of Nina...

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.010
Yes, this is the bridge.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:35.320
<i>This is Lt. Monsha. We think</i>
<i>we've sighted the enemy.</i>

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:37.980
<i>We're gonna check it out.</i>
<i>Oh, and we're taking the Gundam, too.</i>

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:40.460
Huh?! Hey, wait!

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.240
You listening?
The rules are simple.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:02.720
First guy to get a paint round
on the other guy's suit wins.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.180
<i>I'll signal when you start.</i>

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:07.650
<i>You two ready to go?</i>

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:10.020
I'm ready when you are.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:18.430
Okay, here we go!

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.560
Drive carefully <i>and</i> fast!
Go faster!

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:28.970
I <i>am</i> driving fast, Lieutenant!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.370
If we rock too much,
your wounds'll open!

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:35.110
Damn it, if we don't hurry,
it's all over! Now move it!

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:44.480
A GM custom
mass-production type...

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.220
Remarkable for being
totally unremarkable.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:01.510
Too slow!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:07.850
Shit!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.510
You just gonna run
from me, Ensign?!

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:20.020
Dammit, Monsha! Watch it!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.150
Heh! Sorry, guys!

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.400
Not bad, Lieutenant.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:38.370
That prototype moves
faster than I thought.

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.740
All right!

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:42.780
Follow me, Rookie!

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:45.750
All right! Just what
I was waiting for!

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:51.320
The lieutenant's playing it
a little reckless, isn't he?

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:56.160
Typical. I'm more interested in
seeing how well the ensign does.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.620
Ensign Uraki...

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.410
Where is he?

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.730
What the?!

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.800
Above me?!

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.910
Shit!

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.050
Nimble bastard!

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:02.720
I have to win!

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:09.360
Damn!

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.060
Gotcha!

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:18.330
I win!

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:19.740
Damn it!

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:26.280
Wh- Where is he?!

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:28.750
Where'd he go?!

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.450
What the?!

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:51.670
It... It's impossible!
I lost?!

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:55.310
I did it... I did it!

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:56.940
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:03.580
Keith told me everything.
How could you do this?!

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:06.320
L- Lieutenant...

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.950
Just get back to the base!

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:11.290
I'll take care of the rest.
You read me?!

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:12.730
- Yes, sir.
- Right...

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:21.300
One week, solitary confinement.
Understood?

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:23.310
Yes, sir.

00:22:24.010 --> 00:22:25.980
Later, pal.

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:28.340
One week for you, too.
Understood?

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.710
Yeah.

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:33.910
Kou...

00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:46.960
<i>So, Nina and Orville want</i>
<i>to remain on the ship?</i>

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:48.190
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

00:22:48.230 --> 00:22:51.830
<i>Understood. I'll contact</i>
<i>the captain from here.</i>

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:54.670
<i>The rest of the staff</i>
<i>should stay there at the base.</i>

00:22:54.710 --> 00:22:57.540
<i>Whatever happens,</i>
<i>just be careful out there.</i>

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:00.470
Yes, sir. And thank you.

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:07.350
Are you all right, Lieutenant?

00:23:07.390 --> 00:23:10.720
Yeah. I'm not hurt
that badly, sir.

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:13.390
I'm sorry about what happened.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:18.350
Looks like your men may
be hard for me to control.

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:19.960
I have a proposal.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.360
Sir?

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:25.670
I'd like you to be this
ship's company commander.

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:27.670
You... You want <i>me,</i> sir?

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:32.200
Yes. You'd have total authority
for all mobile suit-related matters.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:34.370
Keep a tight rein on things.

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:37.910
Can I assign a rookie
pilot to Unit 1, too?

00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:40.380
That's all up to you.

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:44.390
Thank you, Captain!

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:48.950
This ship is to set course
for Africa immediately!

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:50.900
All hands, prepare for launch!

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:52.860
All hands, prepare for launch!

00:25:12.410 --> 00:25:17.450
<i>Don't come to me just 'cause you're lonely tonight...</i>

00:25:17.450 --> 00:25:22.080
<i>Lonely's only part of your game...</i>

00:25:22.460 --> 00:25:27.880
<i>As long as you live, you must remember one thing...</i>

00:25:27.880 --> 00:25:32.660
<i>Give and take are one and the same...</i>

00:25:32.660 --> 00:25:35.230
<i>So tell me are you ready?</i>

00:25:35.230 --> 00:25:37.900
<i>Really, really ready?</i>

00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:42.410
<i>I don't want your love for one night!</i>

00:25:42.410 --> 00:25:48.200
<i>'Cause I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:25:48.200 --> 00:25:53.060
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near...</i>

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:58.550
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:25:58.550 --> 00:26:03.720
<i>I need the magic when I touch your hand!</i>

00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:08.880
<i>I'm not lookin' for a love affair...</i>

00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:14.050
<i>I need the magic when I hold you near!</i>

00:26:14.050 --> 00:26:19.230
<i>It's more important than a one-night stand...</i>

00:26:19.230 --> 00:26:26.680
<i>I need the magic when I touch...touch your hand...</i>

00:26:46.420 --> 00:26:48.190
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:51.640
The Gundam wanders,
searching for the lost Unit 2.

00:26:51.980 --> 00:26:54.350
It is now in the
distant land of Africa.

00:26:55.630 --> 00:26:58.010
The shimmering waves of heat
over the burning land...

00:26:58.030 --> 00:27:00.130
...only heighten
the crew's unease.

00:27:00.160 --> 00:27:04.120
The pilots' quarrels begin
to take their toll on Uraki.

00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:06.700
As frustration breeds
discord aboard the ship...

00:27:06.700 --> 00:27:09.910
...the ghosts
of Zeon reawaken.

00:27:09.940 --> 00:27:13.200
Will their rage
destroy the <i>Albion?</i>

00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:16.960
ATTACK AND RETREAT
ON THE BURNING SAND
